  "content": [
    {
      "text": "An Alexandrian Jew, an eloquent man and mighty in the scriptures (Acts 18:24–19:1). He received instruction in the gospel at Ephesus from Aquila and Priscilla and then went to Corinth; his name was afterwards connected with one of the disputes that arose there (1 Cor. 1:12; 3:4–6, 22; 16:12). We afterwards hear of him in Crete (Titus 3:13).",
